  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe sinker condition table in the Machine window now has two more inputs for each condition:\n\n- `Condition N wear rate`: a tick box (\"not stated\" when off) and a number field. The tick seeds 0.1.\n- `Condition N notes`: a text field.\n\nThey sit on a second line under the condition row, so the row stays inside the window.\n\nBoth inputs edit the machine draft only. Apply sends the existing undoable `EditMachineApply`, so undo restores the old machine. No new command was added, so no MCP tool is owed.\n\nThe wear-rate check is the check from #1157 (`wear_rate_ok`, a finite ratio from 0 up to but not including 1). The page names a bad value beside the section (\"Apply will refuse: condition N wear: ...\"). Apply refuses it by name, because `LoadMachine` uses the same law.\n\nThe existing Apply tests now wait 10 steps after the scroll, because the taller section needs more frames to settle.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/sinker_machine_tests.rs`)\n\n- `the_condition_row_edits_wear_rate_and_notes_through_one_undoable_apply`\n- `a_bad_wear_rate_is_named_and_refused_like_the_loader_does`\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` passed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Screenshots are owed. This is a UI change and the GUI was not started.\n- No pixel snapshot was run or changed.\n- The wear rate shows no unit lens, because it is a ratio.\n\nChangelog: Sinker machine page: the condition table edits each condition's wear rate and notes (#1381)\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1381\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
